{"author":"rebar review bot","author_email":"rebar-review-bot@rebar.solutions.navateam.com","data":{"body":"## AC5 settled: its subject was REMOVED from this host, not repaired\n\nMeasured directly on 2026-09-20 with the sandbox lifted, so these are real `ENOENT`\nresults rather than denied reads. An earlier pass in this session reported the same paths\nas missing while `~/.local/` was sandbox-blocked; that reading was not trustworthy and is\nsuperseded by what follows. A control probe confirms the difference: `~/.local`,\n`~/.local/state`, `~/.local/bin` and `~/.local/share` all resolve as EXISTING, while every\npath below is genuinely absent.\n\n```\n~/.local/state/rebar-dev                     No such file or directory\n~/.local/state/rebar-dev/releases            No such file or directory\n~/.local/state/rebar-dev/current/sha         No such file or directory\n~/.local/state/rebar-dev/reject-streak       No such file or directory\n~/.local/state/rebar-dev/launchd.err.log     No such file or directory\n~/.local/state/rebar-dev/update.log          No such file or directory\n~/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh             MISSING\n~/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh.pre-ac97.bak MISSING\n```\n\nThe updater was not merely unloaded. The script, its `.pre-ac97.bak` backup created by\nthis ticket's own AC2 fix, its entire state tree, and its LaunchAgent are all gone:\n\n```\n~/Library/LaunchAgents/   com.joeoakhart.agent-config-backup.plist\n                          com.joeoakhart.agent-skills-update.plist\n                          com.joeoakhart.secrets-load.plist\n                          (dir mtime Sep 12 00:54)\nlaunchctl list | grep -iE 'navapbc|rebar'   -> no match\nfind ~ -name 'rebar-dev-update*' -o -name 'com.navapbc.rebar*'   -> no match\nfind ~ -type d -name 'rebar-dev'   -> no match\nfind ~ -name 'local-env-main-tracking*'   -> no match\n```\n\nAll three `com.navapbc.rebar-*` agents that earlier comments recorded at exit 0 —\n`rebar-dev-update`, `rebar-worktree-gc`, `rebar-serena-mirror-update` — are absent.\n`docs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md` is gone as well, with no git history, which is\nexpected for a git-ignored file.\n\n## Why AC5 is marked `[non-codebase]` rather than ticked as fixed\n\nAC5's two checks both pass, but VACUOUSLY. The `5fb693345b0cd...1559` stub is absent\nbecause the whole `releases` tree is absent, and `Directory not empty` cannot appear in a\n`launchd.err.log` that does not exist. That is not evidence the pruner was repaired, and\nrecording it as such would assert something untrue.\n\n## Restore was attempted first and is not available\n\nPer operator decision the preferred path was to restore the updater and verify AC5 against\na live pruner. `~/Desktop/backup` was inspected for that purpose and carries neither\n`.local/` nor `Library/`, so it never captured the updater, its state, or its plist. No\nother copy exists anywhere under `$HOME`. Rebuilding the script from scratch would be\nauthoring a NEW machine-local tool rather than restoring one, and this ticket is not the\nplace for that.\n\n## What this ticket actually fixed, and why it closes as env_integration\n\nThe reported defect was real, root-caused, and fixed. AC1 and AC2 are satisfied by\nevidence already recorded above: the uv pin is now read from the CANDIDATE COMMIT's own\n`pyproject.toml` rather than hardcoded, no absolute path is baked in, PATH order is no\nlonger load-bearing, and the live updater run took `reject-streak` from 122 to 0 while\nadvancing `current` to `6125c5345f01`, ending 201 commits of drift. AC3 was withdrawn by\noperator decision (cross-account SNS not pursued). AC4 was withdrawn from rebar's shipped\nsurface across two rejected changes, 2608 and 3014, and is recorded as `[non-codebase]`.\n\nThe root cause was an exact uv `required-version` pin interacting with the versions\navailable on one host — an environment/integration defect, not a defect in rebar's own\nlogic. Hence `env_integration`.\n\n## Adjacent finding, deliberately NOT tracked here\n\nThis host has had no main-tracking updater since approximately 2026-09-12. The global\n`rebar` symlink was last written Sep 14 19:45. Gates run from a repository worktree venv\nand are unaffected, but anything invoking the global `rebar` gets that older build. If the\nremoval was not deliberate, restoring main-tracking is separate work needing its own\nticket; AGENTS.md places that tooling outside this repository."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789941919550538001,"uuid":"47508da5-246f-42fe-93c1-5831186f4577"}